figures.caption:
Pole structure and contour choices in the ζ \zeta plane for helicity s 2 = + s_{2}=+ , together with the pole crossed during contour deformation. Blue dots denote the right pole families generated by Γ ⁡ [ − ζ , 2 ​ i ​ ν ~ − ζ ] \Gamma[-\zeta,2\mathrm{i}\widetilde{
u}-\zeta] , while red dots denote the left pole families generated by Γ ⁡ [ i ⁡ ( ρ − 1 ) ​ ν ~ + ζ + β χ + 2 , − i ⁡ ( ν ~ + λ ~ ) + ζ ] \Gamma[\mathrm{i}(ho-1)\widetilde{
u}+\zeta+ eta_{\chi}+2,-\mathrm{i}(\widetilde{
u}+\widetilde{\lambda})+\zeta] . We take ρ = 1 ho=1 and β χ = − 1  eta_{\chi}=-1 as an example. The green lines with arrows indicate the integration contours. To separate the left and right pole families, the contour 𝒞 ζ \mathcal{C}_{\zeta} must bend locally to the right, keeping the pole at ζ = i ⁡ ( ν ~ + λ ~ ) \zeta=\mathrm{i}(\widetilde{
u}+\widetilde{\lambda}) to its left. For numerical convenience, we can deform 𝒞 ζ \mathcal{C}_{\zeta} into the vertical contour 𝒞 ζ ′ \mathcal{C}_{\zeta}^{\prime} . This deformation crosses the pole at ζ = i ⁡ ( ν ~ + λ ~ ) \zeta=\mathrm{i}(\widetilde{
u}+\widetilde{\lambda}) , marked by the green circle. When evaluating the integral along 𝒞 ζ ′ \mathcal{C}_{\zeta}^{\prime} , the residue contribution from this pole must therefore be added.

